{"_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"content": "The Brave New World of the Internet", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "From the Future", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 3, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 10, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "B1.2", "type": "level"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"content": " Accurately use information about common technology in communicative situations.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology.", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology.", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology.", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology.", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": "Writes an exchange of written communications about asking for and giving advice on problems with technology or gadgets through the correct use of spelling, grammar, vocabulary, level of formality, cohesion and coherence aspects appropriated to this level.", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology.", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": "Writes an exchange of written communications about asking for and giving advice on problems with technology or gadgets through the correct use of spelling, grammar, vocabulary, level of formality, cohesion and coherence aspects appropriated to this level.", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": "Writes an exchange of written communications about asking for and giving advice on problems with technology or gadgets through the correct use of spelling, grammar, vocabulary, level of formality, cohesion and coherence aspects appropriated to this level.", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"content": "engenn7le10ob03re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": " Talking About the Future", "type": "heading"}, {"content": " You can use four different tenses to talk about the future.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "<ul><li>When you talk about things that are not decided or when you make a decision at the moment of speaking for the future, you use the modal <span class=\"italic\">will</span>.</li>  <li>When you ask about intentions, you use <span class=\"italic\">going to</span>.</li>  <li>When you talk about things that are arranged, on the agenda or booked for the future, you use the Present Continuous tense.</li>  <li>When you talk about schedules or timetables in the future, you use the Simple Present tense.</li></ul>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":5,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Verb Tense\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Example\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\"> Future Tense (Will)</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" <span class=\\\"italic\\\"> The majority of the world population will have access to technology by 2020.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\"> Going to</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" <span class=\\\"italic\\\"> I'm going to show the technological  advances in future computers.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\"> Present Continuous Tense</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" <span class=\\\"italic\\\">  I'm preparing a talk for a conference tomorrow.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\"> Simple Present Tense</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" <span class=\\\"italic\\\"> There is a conference next week on this subject. </span>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}", "type": "table"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Subject and Object Relative Clauses", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "When you want to make it clear which person or thing you are talking about, you use a relative clause.<br/><br/>  You can begin a relative clause with <span class=\"italic\">who</span> for people, <span class=\"italic\">which</span> for things or <span class=\"italic\">that</span> for either people or things.<br/><br/>  In spoken English you usually use <span class=\"italic\">that</span>, rather than <span class=\"italic\">which</span> or <span class=\"italic\">who</span>.<br/><br/>  You put the relative clause immediately after the noun it talks about.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "A subject relative clause describes the subject of the clause.<br/> <span class=\"strong\">Example</span>:<br/> <span class=\"italic\">The man who called wanted to speak to Tom.</span> Which man? The man who called. <br/>The clause <span class=\"italic\">who called</span> immediately follows man - the noun it describes.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "An object relative clause describes the object of the clause.<br/> <span class=\"strong\">Example</span>:<br/>  <span class=\"italic\">Can you return the book that I lent you?</span> Which book? The book I lent you.<br/>The clause <span class=\"italic\">that I lent you</span> immediately follows book - the noun it describes.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":5,\"columns\":4,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Example\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Clause\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Relative connector\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Type of Relative Clause\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"> The world population will have access to technology by 2020, which is only a few years away!\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" which is only a few years away\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" <span class=\\\"strong\\\"> which</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" <span class=\\\"strong\\\"> subject</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">  We're closing the gap between the people who have no computer literacy skills and those who own several devices.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"who have no computer literacy skills; who own several devices\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" <span class=\\\"strong\\\">who</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" <span class=\\\"strong\\\"> subject</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"> Google and Microsoft are giving away computers that kids in poor countries can use at school.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" that kids in poor countries can use\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" <span class=\\\"strong\\\">that</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" <span class=\\\"strong\\\">object</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">  I'm going to show the advances that tech companies are making in this field.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"that tech companies are making in this field\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" <span class=\\\"strong\\\">that</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" <span class=\\\"strong\\\">object</span>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}", "type": "table"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "conference", "type": "name"}, {"content": " a formal meeting for discussion", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: There is a conference next week on the subject of access to technology.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le10ob03aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": " These are words you hear in a conversation about the future of computers.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "advance", "type": "name"}, {"content": "technological progress", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I'm going to talk about advances in new technologies.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le10ob03aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "field", "type": "name"}, {"content": "subject of study", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I'm going to show the advances that tech companies are making in this field.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le10ob03aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "initiative", "type": "name"}, {"content": "an idea meant to improve a situation", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: This is an initiative that more people should know about!", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le10ob03aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to close the gap", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to reduce a disparity between people", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: We're closing the gap between the people who have no computer literacy skills and those who own several devices.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le10ob03aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "overwhelming", "type": "name"}, {"content": "very great; very strong", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The overwhelming majority of the world population will have access to technology by 2020.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le10ob03aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "RAM", "type": "name"}, {"content": "Random Access Memory; the processing power of a computer", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I think my phone has more RAM than the laptop that I used in college!", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le10ob03aud07", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "Go online. Find information about new<br> technologies and initiatives to improve people's lives.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Write a list of 4 technologies you found <br> interesting or original.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Briefly explain why you think each <br> technology is&nbsp;important, and why you think they will help improve people's lives.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Use the chart below to take notes.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Compare your list with your partner and ask questions about their activities.<br/><br/><br/>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":5,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Technology\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"How will it improve people's lives?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"&nbsp;\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"&nbsp;\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"&nbsp;\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"&nbsp;\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"&nbsp;\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"&nbsp;\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"&nbsp;\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"&nbsp;\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}", "type": "table"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I write about new technologies.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I talk about future actions.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I ask for clarification about complex ideas with a partner.", "type": "text"}]}], "labs": [{"exercises": [{"template_override": 1, "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"content": " I can talk about technology.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " I can talk about future action. ", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " I can express complex statements using words like who, that or which.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " Where do you think you will be in the next five years? What will you do?", "type": "Free Header Item"}, {"content": " Do you have electronic devices at home? What are they?", "type": "Free Header Item"}]}, {"type": "group", "contents": [{"content": "Welcome", "type": "group_name"}]}, {"content": {"allowed_attempts": 2, "incorrect_feedback": [{"content": "try again", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Maybe next time", "type": "text"}], "correct_feedback": "Correct", "attempt_feedback": [{"content": "You have 2 tries", "type": "text"}, {"content": "you have 1 attempt left", "type": "text"}]}, "type": "feedback"}, {"content": "Ask your partner:", "type": "free_header_text"}, {"content": " Technology is connecting people all over the world. Welcome to the future